  "Question": "If \\((3x-1)^7=a_7x^7+a_6x^6+\\cdots+a_0,\\) then \\(a_7+a_6+\\cdots+a_0\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(64\\)",
    "D": "\\(-64\\)",
    "E": "\\(128\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "To turn the polynomial into the sum of its coefficients, set \\(x=1\\). Every power of \\(x\\) then equals \\(1\\), so the given identity yields\n\\[\na_7+a_6+\\cdots+a_0=(3\\cdot1-1)^7=2^7=128.\n\\]\nThus the coefficient sum is \\(128\\), choice E.",
